From: flippy <flippy@thebe.tail087954.ts.net>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:38:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] porg: label the AirPlay session-interrupt property

jetsontv.airplay.interrupt is written by the controlling app to end the
current AirPlay session when another app takes audio focus for good,
and watched by init, which restarts the daemon. It is an event rather
than a setting, so it is not persistent, and it takes the same
shairport_prop label as the enable flag -- the app can already set that
type, and nothing else should.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ib90eaeb9e645e7138eb64fa78ae9ee6269b6e2c3
---
 sepolicy/private/property_contexts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sepolicy/private/property_contexts b/sepolicy/private/property_contexts
index 7916278..bca45bf 100644
--- a/sepolicy/private/property_contexts
+++ b/sepolicy/private/property_contexts
@@ -1 +1,3 @@
 persist.jetsontv.airplay.    u:object_r:shairport_prop:s0
+# The session-interrupt event: set by the controlling app, watched by init.
+jetsontv.airplay.            u:object_r:shairport_prop:s0
-- 
